1.1.evidence:
COPY
REGENT OF KEPAHIANG
BENGKULU PROVINCE
REGIONAL REGULATION OF KEPAHIANG REGENCY NUMBER 10 OF 2016
CONCERNING
PROTECTION OF WOMEN AND CHILDREN
AGAINST ACTS OF VIOLENCE
BY THE GRACE OF GOD ALMIGHTY
REGENT OF KEPAHIANG,

Considering : a. that every citizen has the right to survival, growth, and development, to obtain protection of personal self, honor and dignity as a complete human being in family life, society, nation and state;
b. that every citizen has the right to be free from torture or treatment that degrades human dignity and has the right to obtain security and freedom from all forms of violence and discrimination;
c. that all forms of acts of violence against women and children constitute violations of human rights so that their dignity and honor need to be protected and their right to life guaranteed in accordance with their nature and destiny without discrimination;
d. that violence against women and children in Kepahiang Regency continues to increase both in quantity and quality, so that prevention, protection, recovery and law enforcement efforts are needed;
e. that legislation regarding the protection of women and children victims of violence requires the support of regulations and institutional mechanisms at the Kepahiang Regency level that can guarantee its implementation;
f. that based on the considerations as referred to in letter a, letter b, letter c, letter d and letter e, it is necessary to establish a Regional Regulation of Kepahiang concerning the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence;

In View of : 1. Article 18 Paragraph (6) of the 1945 Constitution of the Republic of Indonesia;
2. Law Number 7 of 1984 concerning Ratification of the Convention on the Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women (Convention on The Elimination of All Forms of Discrimination Against Women) (State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia of 1984 Number 29, Supplement to the State Gazette of the Republic of Indonesia Number 3277);
